course: world
lesson: 25
title: Life cycles
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Every living thing goes through a life cycle: it begins, grows, becomes an adult, makes young of its own, and in the end dies, while its young start the cycle again.
explain: A frog starts as an egg in a pond, hatches into a tadpole that swims and breathes with gills, then grows legs, loses its tail and becomes a frog that can live on land.
explain: A butterfly has four very different stages: egg, caterpillar (larva), chrysalis (pupa) and adult; this big change is called metamorphosis.
explain: A chicken hatches from an egg as a fluffy chick that already looks like a small hen, and simply grows; a bean plant grows from a seed into a plant that flowers and makes new beans.
explain: A caterpillar eats and eats, growing many times bigger, then inside the chrysalis its body is rebuilt into a butterfly with wings.
fact: A life cycle is the series of changes a living thing goes through from birth to adult and new young.
fact: A frog's life cycle is egg, tadpole, froglet and adult frog.
fact: Frogs lay their eggs in clumps of clear jelly with a black dot in each egg; this is called frogspawn.
fact: Tadpoles live in water and breathe with gills.
fact: Adult frogs breathe with lungs and through their skin.
fact: A butterfly's life cycle is egg, caterpillar, chrysalis and adult butterfly.
fact: Metamorphosis is a big change in body shape during an animal's life; frogs, butterflies, beetles and bees all go through it.
fact: A caterpillar does most of the eating and growing in a butterfly's life.
fact: A chicken's life cycle is egg, chick and adult hen or rooster.
fact: A hen's egg must be kept warm for about three weeks before the chick hatches.
fact: A bean plant's life cycle is seed, seedling, adult plant with flowers, and pods with new seeds.
fact: When a seed starts to grow it is called germination; it needs water, air and warmth.
fact: Most seeds do not need light to germinate, because they use their own food store at first.
exercise: What hatches from a frog's egg? | A tadpole | A froglet | A caterpillar | A small adult frog
exercise: How does a tadpole breathe? | With gills | With lungs | Through its tail | It does not breathe
exercise: What are the four stages of a butterfly's life? | Egg, caterpillar, chrysalis, butterfly | Egg, tadpole, froglet, butterfly | Seed, caterpillar, cocoon, moth | Egg, chick, chrysalis, butterfly
exercise: What is another name for a caterpillar? | A larva | A chrysalis | A tadpole | A young nymph
exercise: What happens inside a chrysalis? | The body is rebuilt into a butterfly | The caterpillar sleeps and stays the same | The butterfly lays its eggs | The caterpillar eats leaves inside it
exercise: What is metamorphosis? | A big change in body shape during life | An animal moving to a warm place | An animal sleeping through the winter | A plant making food from light
exercise: In which stage does a butterfly do most of its growing? | The caterpillar | The egg | The chrysalis | The adult butterfly
exercise: What does a chick look like when it hatches? | Like a small, fluffy hen | Like a worm with no legs | Like a tadpole with a tail | Like a featherless ball
exercise: What must happen to a hen's egg for a chick to grow inside? | It must be kept warm | It must be kept in water | It must be kept in light | It must be kept cold
exercise: What does a seed need to germinate? | Water, air and warmth | Darkness, soil and salt | Light, snow and wind | Sugar, soil and cold
exercise: What does a frog lose as it grows from a tadpole? | Its tail | Its legs | Its eyes | Its lungs
exercise: What comes after the seedling stage of a bean plant? | An adult plant with flowers | A seed in the soil | A dry, empty pod | A chrysalis on a leaf
exercise: Where do frogs usually lay their eggs? | In water | In a nest in a tree | Under hot sand | Inside a cocoon
exercise: Why can a seed sprout in the dark soil? | It uses its own stored food at first | It makes food without any light | It eats the soil around it | It gets light through the soil
test: A child finds jelly with black dots in a pond in spring. What will the dots become first? | Tadpoles | Frogs | Fish | Caterpillars
test: Which animal does NOT go through metamorphosis? | A chicken | A frog | A butterfly | A beetle
test: A caterpillar stops eating and hangs still in a hard case. What stage is it in? | Pupa | Larva | Embryo | Adult
test: Beans are put on wet cotton in a dark cupboard and also sprout. What does this show? | Germination does not need light | Beans need no water at all | Seeds need darkness to live | Cotton feeds the seeds
test: Which order is right for a frog? | Egg, tadpole, froglet, frog | Tadpole, egg, frog, froglet | Egg, froglet, tadpole, frog | Frog, tadpole, egg, froglet
test: Why can a young frog leave the water but a young tadpole cannot? | The frog has lungs and legs | The tadpole is afraid of land | The frog has bigger gills | The tadpole has no eyes yet
test: What do the new beans in a bean pod start? | A new life cycle | A new chrysalis | A new tadpole | A new flower bud
test: Dry beans have been kept in a jar for a year without growing. Why? | They had no water | They had no sunlight | They had no garden soil | They had no fertiliser
test: Which is true about a butterfly and its caterpillar? | They are the same animal at different stages | They are two different kinds of animal | The caterpillar is the butterfly's food | The butterfly turns back into a caterpillar
test: whats a tadpole turn into | A frog | A small fish | A newt only | A water beetle
test: how long's a hen sit on her eggs before they hatch | About three weeks | About three days | About three months | About one week
test: Leo says the caterpillar sleeps in the chrysalis and then just grows wings. true? | No, its whole body changes shape inside, that's metamorphosis | Yes, it just grows wings while it sleeps | Yes, it only adds wings and stays the same | No, it stays a caterpillar for life
test: my sister reckons seeds need light to start growing. right? | No, most use their own food store and need water, air and warmth | Yes, all seeds need bright light to sprout | Yes, a seed in the dark can never grow | No, seeds need only soil to start growing
exam: State, in the correct order, the stages in the life cycle of a frog. | Egg, tadpole, froglet, adult frog | Tadpole, egg, froglet, adult frog | Egg, froglet, tadpole, adult frog | Egg, caterpillar, chrysalis, adult frog
exam: Which of the following is designated by the term metamorphosis? | A great alteration in body shape during an animal's life | The laying of eggs by an adult animal | The long winter sleep of an animal | The journey of an animal to warmer lands
exam: Identify the stage of a butterfly's life cycle in which the greater part of feeding and growth occurs. | The caterpillar | The egg | The chrysalis | The adult butterfly
exam: Select the response that is consistent with the established facts concerning the germination of most seeds. | It requires water, air and warmth, but not light | It requires light, but not water | It requires soil rich in sugar | It requires darkness and the absence of air
